ntdll: a top-down allocation with no limit stays below the image views
(docs/design/wine-unix.md, section 4, "MEM_TOP_DOWN with no limit").

Why: map_view searches a request with no limit_high from
min(user_space_limit, host_addr_space_limit), 16 GiB here, down
(dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c L2287-2295), so a top-down allocation would
grow the wasm memory to 16 GiB. Guest code gets there through
NtAllocateVirtualMemory with MEM_TOP_DOWN and no zero bits, which passes
no limit (L5223-5228; unix_private.h L527).

- map_view (virtual.c): a top-down request with no limit_high first
  searches below a ceiling, the end of the highest image view rounded up
  to 64 KiB (top_down_ceiling, new): in the reserved areas, then between
  the views, as Wine's own search does. Only if nothing fits there does it
  go on to Wine's search of the full range. With no image view there is no
  ceiling.
- Images never get there: map_image_view always passes a limit_high
  (L3329), and so does the Unix side's PEB and TEB block below 2 GiB
  (L4054-4055).

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -2273,6 +2273,29 @@
     return status;
 }
 
+#ifdef __wasm64__
+/***********************************************************************
+ *           top_down_ceiling
+ *
+ * Tempwind (wine-unix.md, section 4): the end of the highest image view,
+ * rounded up to 64 KiB, or NULL with no image view.
+ * virtual_mutex must be held by caller.
+ */
+static void *top_down_ceiling(void)
+{
+    struct wine_rb_entry *ptr;
+
+    for (ptr = rb_tail( views_tree.root ); ptr; ptr = rb_prev( ptr ))
+    {
+        struct file_view *view = WINE_RB_ENTRY_VALUE( ptr, struct file_view, entry );
+
+        if (view->protect & SEC_IMAGE)
+            return (void *)(((UINT_PTR)view->base + view->size + granularity_mask) & ~granularity_mask);
+    }
+    return NULL;
+}
+#endif
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *           map_view
  *
@@ -2339,6 +2362,25 @@
         if (limit_low && (void *)limit_low > start) start = (void *)limit_low;
         if (limit_high && (void *)limit_high < end) end = (char *)limit_high + 1;
 
+#ifdef __wasm64__
+        /* Tempwind (wine-unix.md, section 4): with no limit_high, a top-down
+         * search starts at 16 GiB and would grow the memory there. It first
+         * searches below the image views; only if nothing fits does it go on
+         * as Wine does. */
+        if (top_down && !limit_high)
+        {
+            void *ceiling = top_down_ceiling();
+
+            if (ceiling > start && ceiling < end &&
+                ((ptr = map_reserved_area( start, ceiling, host_size, top_down, unix_prot, align_mask )) ||
+                 (ptr = map_free_area( start, ceiling, host_size, top_down, unix_prot, align_mask ))))
+            {
+                TRACE( "got mem below the image views %p-%p\n", ptr, (char *)ptr + size );
+                goto done;
+            }
+        }
+#endif
+
         if ((ptr = map_reserved_area( start, end, host_size, top_down, unix_prot, align_mask )))
         {
             TRACE( "got mem in reserved area %p-%p\n", ptr, (char *)ptr + size );
